# NOTE: cherry-picked patches are only reachable through the branches that hold
# them. refs/heads/franken-pins anchors every commit below so the rebuild keeps
# working after a feature branch is deleted. Refresh it whenever this file changes:
#   git commit-tree $(git write-tree) -p <sha> -p <sha> ... | xargs git push origin HEAD:franken-pins
#
# franken-master manifest — ordered feature patches, cherry-picked onto master.
# Columns: <commit> <owning-branch> <subject>
# Rebuild: scripts/rebuild-franken.sh
# A patch leaves this file once it merges upstream.
#
# Order is dependency order. stack/cloudfront-routing carries two commits:
# behavior routing needs origin_domain_names from the CF-origins patch, so the
# pair must stay adjacent and in this order.
